1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
The better question came out of a long argument about authority: who has the right to make a decision that will outlive the person who makes it?

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,218
“We think about the election and not about the ten years after it,” the chair said.

3
00:00:14,218 --> 00:00:21,292
“A ruling that nobody can revise is not a rule; it is a veto on the future.”

4
00:00:21,292 --> 00:00:26,326
The sense of the room was that the past had been treated as a guarantee.

5
00:00:26,326 --> 00:00:33,579
“Our planning has been built on one assumption, and the assumption is a fashion,” Maya wrote.

6
00:00:33,579 --> 00:00:42,967
“We are responsible for a selection of facts, not for all of them, and the waste is in the ones we discarded.”

7
00:00:42,967 --> 00:00:54,714
The hearing produced a representation of the risk that nobody had prepared for: a variable that was treated as secondary, and a hedge that had become the whole venture.

8
00:00:54,714 --> 00:01:00,083
“Be conscious of the motivation behind a number,” the auditor said.

9
00:01:00,083 --> 00:01:04,847
“A coherent report can still be a rude one.”

10
00:01:04,847 --> 00:01:11,761
The abstract part of the question was the hardest: what kind of thinking do we reward?

11
00:01:11,761 --> 00:01:25,713
A cue from the dial, an inspiration from the sole survivor of the last flood, and a decision made in peril: the room had a dozen answers and no method for choosing between them.

12
00:01:25,713 --> 00:01:30,382
“Do not speculate about the dead,” the boatman said.

13
00:01:30,382 --> 00:01:46,534
“Consider the living.” The daring part of the proposal was to publish the disagreement itself, with the condensation of six months of argument on a single page, and the careful record of who had said what.

14
00:01:46,534 --> 00:01:53,717
Therefore the better question was not what the group should decide, but who should be able to revise it.

15
00:01:53,717 --> 00:02:03,475
The price of that question was high, the good and the bad answers would both be carried forward, and the moment had arrived to write it down.

16
00:02:03,475 --> 00:02:10,698
Against the history of the valley, the value of a selective record was the only thing we could find.

17
00:02:10,698 --> 00:02:21,201
The mind does not die with an author, and then the archive must answer for itself; the sole and the ruling were the same word in a different sense.

18
00:02:21,201 --> 00:02:28,987
We had to find a way to keep the mind of the project alive after its authors moved on.
